      "question": "Yun had 20 paperclips initially, but then lost 12. Marion has 1/4 more than what Yun currently has, plus 7. How many paperclips does Marion have?",
      "selected_index": 3,
      "majority_index": 1,
      "selected_final_answer": "17",
      "reference_final_answer": "9",
      "all_candidate_final_answers": [
        "9",
        "17",
        "17",
        "17"
      ],
      "correct_candidate_indices": [
        0
      ],
      "confidence": 0.954735443709999,
      "selected_text": "We are given the following:\n\n- Yun had **20 paperclips** initially.\n- Then lost **12**, so **Yun currently has** $ 20 - 12 = 8 $ paperclips.\n\n- Marion has **$ \\frac{1}{4} $ more than what Yun currently has, plus 7**.\n\nSo, we calculate:\n\n$$\n\\text{Marion's paperclips} = 8 + \\left( \\frac{1}{4} \\times 8 \\right) + 7\n$$\n\n$$\n= 8 + 2 + 7 = 17\n$$\n\n### Final Answer:\n$$\n\\boxed{17}\n$$",
      "attribution_status": "Observed answer/selection mismatch only; intermediate reasoning has not been manually verified. No process-supervision label was created."
