      "id": "gsm8k:c7e31f077e16c06ce1854ed8edc5aaf8be1c629e558c151b7d32b78cb867f158",
      "question": "Megan bought 2 dozen eggs. As she was walking to her car, she dropped a tray of eggs. 3 eggs broke, and twice as many cracked. What is the difference between the eggs that are still in perfect condition and those that are cracked?",
      "selected_index": 2,
      "majority_index": 0,
      "selected_final_answer": "6",
      "reference_final_answer": "9",
      "all_candidate_final_answers": [
        "9",
        "18",
        "6",
        null
      ],
      "correct_candidate_indices": [
        0
      ],
      "confidence": 0.4466787342807039,
      "selected_text": "Megan bought 2 dozen eggs, which is **24 eggs**. She dropped a tray of eggs, and **3 eggs broke**, and **twice as many cracked**, meaning **6 eggs cracked**.\n\n- Perfect condition: $ 24 - 3 - 6 = 15 $ eggs.\n- Cracked: $ 3 + 6 = 9 $ eggs.\n\nThe difference between the eggs that are still in perfect condition and those that are cracked is:\n\n$$\n15 - 9 = \\boxed{6}\n$$\n\n#### <numeric answer> 6",
      "attribution_status": "Observed answer/selection mismatch only; intermediate reasoning has not been manually verified. No process-supervision label was created."
    },
    {
      "category": "model correct, majority wrong",
      "validation_index": 3,
      "id": "gsm8k:e0bce5638f28ceb61a610767278059aec4a642fdcd584761a2df8491c7ef6c46",
      "question": "Jay went to watch a singer in a one hour 20 minutes concert.  If there was a 10-minute intermission, and all the songs were 5 minutes except for one song that lasted 10 minutes, how many songs did she sing?",
      "selected_index": 2,
      "majority_index": 0,
      "selected_final_answer": "13",
      "reference_final_answer": "13",
      "all_candidate_final_answers": [
        "16",
        "14",
        "13",
        "12"
      ],
      "correct_candidate_indices": [
        2
      ],
      "confidence": 0.5619641519096908,
      "selected_text": "Jay attended a concert that started at 9:00 AM and ended at 9:40 AM. This is a **1-hour 20-minute** concert, which means the total duration is:\n\n$$\n60 + 20 = 80 \\text{ minutes}\n$$\n\nThe concert includes an **intermission** of 10 minutes, so the actual time she sang is:\n\n$$\n80 - 10 = 70 \\text{ minutes}\n$$\n\nEach song is **5 minutes** except for **one song that lasted 10 minutes**. Let\u2019s denote the number of songs she sang as $ x $.\n\n- The time taken for the **other $ x - 1 $** songs is $ 5(x - 1) $ minutes.\n- The time for the **10-minute song** is 10 minutes.\n\nSo the total time is:\n\n$$\n5(x - 1) + 10 = 70\n$$\n\nSolving:\n\n$$\n5x - 5 + 10 = 70 \\\\\n5x + 5 = 70 \\\\\n5x = 65 \\\\\nx = 13\n$$\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{13}\n$$",
      "attribution_status": "Observed answer/selection mismatch only; intermediate reasoning has not been manually verified. No process-supervision label was created."
    },
